$\begin{align}
\text{vertex's }r\text{-coordinate}&=\dfrac{(\goldD{12})+(\goldD{-3})}{2}
\\\\
&=\blueD{\dfrac{9}{2}}
\end{align}$

Now we can find the vertex's $y$-coordinate by evaluating $f\left(\blueD{\dfrac{9}{2}}\right)$:

$\begin{align}
f\left(\blueD{\dfrac{9}{2}}\right)&=-\left(\blueD{\dfrac{9}{2}}-12\right)\left(\blueD{\dfrac{9}{2}}+3\right)
\\\\
&=-\left(-\dfrac{15}{2}\right)\left(\dfrac{15}{2}\right)
\\\\
&=\dfrac{225}{4}
\end{align}$
